stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Collecting: LR1 the previous revision closes and a new one opens
    Collecting --> Drafted: LR2 the ledger owner freezes the intake and proposes IDs
    Drafted --> Collecting: LR3 a proposed row is sent back for capture work
    Drafted --> Reviewed: LR4 each new row has a grader and a separate re-checker
    Reviewed --> Published: LR5 the revision is issued with its number and date
    Published --> Reconciled: LR6 census re-counted, crosswalk re-run, guards written, backlog re-sorted
    Reconciled --> [*]: the revision closes and LR1 opens the next
    Reconciled --> Collecting: LR7 a post-conditions check fails and its item returns to intake

    note right of Drafted
        IDs are proposed here and nowhere else.
        A section that mints one fails lint L-03.
    end note

    note right of Published
        Identity is permanent from this point.
        A published ID is never edited, reused
        or renumbered, even if the row is later killed.
    end note

    note right of Reconciled
        The revision is not done when the rows land.
        It is done when the counts, the crosswalk,
        the guards and the backlog agree with it.
    end note
